mac-uniden-bcd325p2 is unofficial community software. It is not affiliated with,
sponsored by, or endorsed by Uniden. Uniden and BCD325P2 identify the hardware
with which the software interoperates.

Protocol and implementation references:
- Uniden BCD325P2 Remote Protocol v1.02:
  https://info.uniden.com/twiki/pub/UnidenMan4/BCD325P2FirmwareUpdate/BCD325P2_Remote_Protocol_ver_1_02.pdf
- Uniden BCD325P2 owner manual:
  https://www.uniden.info/download/ompdf/BCD325P2om.pdf
- Chrome Web Serial documentation:
  https://developer.chrome.com/docs/capabilities/serial
- Brad Town's browser-based Uniden scanner work, consulted during the initial
  investigation of programming on a Mac:
  https://bradtown.com/uniden_scanner/
- Model Context Protocol specification:
  https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25

Vendor manuals, third-party frequency databases and personal scanner records
are not distributed with this project. The MIT license covers the project code
and original documentation, not independently owned source materials linked
from plans or documentation. Check source-specific terms before redistributing
channel datasets. NOAA example frequencies illustrate a public weather service;
they do not predict local reception.
